<title>SINGAPORE: Jaya half year net profit up 22 pct.</title>
<headline>Jaya half year net profit up 22 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year to December 31 1996</p>
<p>	   (in millions of Singapore dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit	    3.54    vs    2.89</p>
<p>    Dividend (cts)	0.50    vs    0.50</p>
<p>    Group share (cts)   2.53    vs    2.10</p>
<p>    Turnover	     43.87    vs   39.43</p>
<p>    Other income	  6.04    vs    1.72</p>
<p>    Interest expense    2.64    vs    3.13</p>
<p>    Exceptional items  (0.80)   vs    nil</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		 3.05    vs    1.78</p>
<p>    Associates	    1.32    vs    2.05</p>
<p>    Tax		     0.32    vs    0.61</p>
<p>    Minorities	   (0.51)   vs   (0.32)</p>
<p>Dividend pay/ reg - April 17 1997/ April 8 1997</p>
<p>Note - Marine based Jaya Holdings Ltd said revenues from shipbuilding/repair were higher due to more works at its Indonesian Batam yard.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
</text>
